      "facts": [
        "The step ceiling of a root turn: a backstop for a turn that never stops, not a work limit. A turn that has stalled ends well before it; see packages/agent-runtime/src/util/turn-progress.ts. Keep it under MAX_AGENT_STEP_ROWS, or a long turn loses its later step rows.",
        "A spawned agent's ceiling, whatever its parent's. Held apart from the root's because every root step can spawn several of these, so raising it multiplies the worst case of a turn.",
        "Root turns only. A subagent keeps its own step ceiling, and most are read-only by design. A programmatic agent's work happens outside the steps recorded here, so the count would miss it.",
        "Ends as a finished turn, not a failed one: nothing broke, and a Mission reads this as the turn's last word when it decides what's next.",
        "Consecutive model steps with no progress that end a root turn. Far above the identical-call guards' thresholds because it matches a broader shape, so a false stop has to be much less likely, and a model polling a slow build with unchanged output has to survive it.",
        "Bookkeeping, not work: a new to-do list is not a new fact about the task."
      ],
